TITLE:: RCMidi
summary:: MIDI CC control of a song, with 14-bit fine pairing
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCSong, Classes/RCKeyboardState

DESCRIPTION::
The proto-library's code::control_synth:: / code::control_midi:: / code::control_attribute::. Every MIDIdef made here is remembered by name and freed by link::#-free:: / link::#-freeAll::. code::fine: true:: pairs cc with cc + 32 (LSB).

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: findSrcId
uid of a MIDI source by name; nil with a warning when absent (the mapping then listens to all sources).

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: control
argument:: name
argument:: ccNum
argument:: chan
argument:: deviceName
argument:: valFunc
Maps the raw value (0..127, fractional with fine).
argument:: action
Receives code::(value, raw)::.
argument:: fine
argument:: throttle
Seconds, nil by default (every message fires). A knob turn sends tens of messages per second, twice as many with code::fine::, and an action over a whole batch (code::batch.editAttr::) costs milliseconds each, which starves the clock: with a throttle the first message fires at once, the ones arriving within the window are swallowed and the last of them fires when the window closes, re-arming while messages keep coming. 0.02 to 0.05 s is inaudible on a knob.
METHOD:: controlSynth
argument:: synth
argument:: attr
nil sets the value itself (buses).
argument:: setNothing
argument:: throttle
As for link::#-control::.
METHOD:: controlAttribute
code::object[key] = value:: for dictionaries, code::object.key_(value):: otherwise.
argument:: throttle
As for link::#-control::.
METHOD:: free
argument:: name
METHOD:: freeAll
